From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 23:04:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/12] LvglDisplayEngineDxe: Redesign the setup UI as System
 Preferences

Lay the setup UI out like the System Preferences of macOS, in a dark
theme: a #121212 desktop, #2C2C2C windows and icons, a #007AFF accent.

- A menu bar across the top of the screen: a symbol, the setup title and
  the device model on the left; Secure Boot, USB storage, battery, date
  and time on the right. A dock of key hints floats above the bottom
  edge.
- The front page is a grid of icons on the desktop: one rounded square
  per entry, with a light shadow and a colored symbol, and the label
  below it. The arrow keys move between the icons in all four directions
  and a light-blue ring marks the focus; the help of the focused entry
  is shown below the grid. The categories of the setup menu and the other
  settings come first, then, after a divider, the boot entries and
  reboot. Above the grid, an overview of the machine: a drawing of the
  laptop, the model and the banner lines (firmware, processor, memory,
  battery).
- Every other form is a window with a gray title bar: window controls
  (decorative; the close control marks unsaved changes), a back button
  (ESC) and the centered title. Settings are grouped on rounded cards,
  one per section, next to a help card. Menus whose entries all open
  other forms (System Configuration) are laid out in titled areas, in
  columns.
- Check boxes are switches, one-of questions open a drop-down menu, and
  dialogs are alerts with a symbol. Read-only strings show their value
  like text lines. Help texts are reflowed for the help card: the line
  breaks of the 80-column text UI are joined within a sentence.

Sizes, colors and fonts come from LvglTheme.h and follow the UI scale.
Only the built-in Montserrat fonts and LVGL symbols are used, without
images or blur: the shadows of the windows, the dock and the icons are
LVGL box shadows.

